---
import SectionEyebrow from './SectionEyebrow.astro';

const migrationGuideUrl = 'https://github.com/cngxjs/compodocx/blob/develop/MIGRATION.md';
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-24" aria-labelledby="migration-heading">
  <SectionEyebrow text="Migration" />
  <aside class="bg-cdx-bg-elevated border-cdx-primary mt-3 rounded-r-xl border-l-4 p-8 sm:p-10">
    <h2
      id="migration-heading"
      class="text-cdx-text text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl"
    >
      Coming from compodoc?
    </h2>
    <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary mt-3 max-w-2xl">
      compodocx is a near-drop-in successor — same surface, modern internals. Most projects migrate
      in a single PR.
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <li class="text-sm">
        <p class="text-cdx-text font-semibold">CLI alias compatible</p>
        <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">
          Existing
          <code class="text-cdx-text bg-cdx-bg-alt rounded px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs"
            >compodoc</code
          >
          scripts run unchanged — the binary registers both names.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="text-sm">
        <p class="text-cdx-text font-semibold">JS template overrides</p>
        <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">
          Custom templates become JS partials returning HTML strings. No Handlebars helpers, no
          partials registry — just <code
            class="text-cdx-text bg-cdx-bg-alt rounded px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs"
            >module.exports = (data, helpers) =&gt; '...'</code
          >.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="text-sm">
        <p class="text-cdx-text font-semibold">Migrate sub-CLI</p>
        <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">
          <code class="text-cdx-text bg-cdx-bg-alt rounded px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs"
            >compodocx migrate</code
          >
          ports Handlebars templates and CSS — subcommands for inspecting, single files, full template
          folders, and stylesheets.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <a
      href={migrationGuideUrl}
      rel="noopener"
      target="_blank"
      class="text-cdx-primary hover:text-cdx-primary-hover mt-8 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium"
    >
      Read the migration guide
      <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
  </aside>
</section>
